  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "After rank eight fighting stops at Heavenly Lotus Sect, three Immortal Gu Houses hover over the ruined field: Canary Pavilion, Yue Yang Palace, and the rank eight Heavenly Pool. Shadow Sect’s group focuses on Heavenly Pool, then pulls back while the three houses chase.",
      "chapters": [
        1000
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_lotus_sect",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "house_yue_yang_palace",
        "loc_heavenly_pool",
        "fac_shadow_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Shi Ge, Mu Ling Lan, and Shi Zheng Yi later find an Immortal Gu House that is an exquisite small pavilion with countless bird cages and continuous bird song, named as Heavenly Lotus Sect’s Canary Pavilion. Shi Ge treats it as a good choice for the Northern Plains attack because it specializes in capturing flying beasts and can move quickly. Shi Zheng Yi lists Canary Pavilion with Yue Yang Palace and Heavenly Pool when asking whether Heavenly Lotus Sect has a fourth Immortal Gu House.",
      "chapters": [
        1233
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "flying-beast-specialty",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_shi_ge",
        "char_mu_ling_lan",
        "char_shi_zheng_yi",
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavenly Lotus Sect’s Canary Pavilion joins Wind Cloud Manor’s Wind Sweeping Building and Combat Immortal Sect’s Edge Link Camp when three rank eight Gu Immortals lead a rescue force into black heaven. It is small and exquisite and filled with liveliness. In the approach formation it holds the rear watch, then takes a turn at the front after Edge Link Camp and Wind Sweeping Building have led stretches of the tunnel through the heavenly wind qi wall.",
      "chapters": [
        1239
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "black-heaven-rescue",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_wind_cloud_manor",
        "house_wind_sweeping_building",
        "fac_combat_immortal_sect",
        "house_edge_link_camp",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After a star cloud storm, Wei Ling Yang leads Canary Pavilion out with Edge Link Camp into a sky chief ambush; half of Canary Pavilion is completely unstable when the three houses break free.",
      "chapters": [
        1246
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sky-chief-ambush",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_wei_ling_yang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the spaceless tunnel collapse, Myriad Tidal Dragon controls Canary Pavilion when a giant hole swallows it.",
      "chapters": [
        1249
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tunnel-collapse",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_myriad_tidal_dragon"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Canary Pavilion later reappears cracked but fighting beside Wind Sweeping Building against Luck Suppression Heavenly Palace, giving off hundreds of canaries singing together and moving with high agility, while Myriad Tidal Dragon controls Wind Sweeping Building and also uses Canary Pavilion in that restriction.",
      "chapters": [
        1267
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "restriction-battle",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_luck_suppression_heavenly_palace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Canary Pavilion is a named Immortal Gu House. It is mobile equipment of Heavenly Lotus Sect, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "restriction-battle",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "At Emperor City, Canary Pavilion is one of Heavenly Lotus Sect’s five Immortal Gu Houses and opens as the same small pavilion with hanging bird cages. It unlocks cages and sends Molten Flame Birds, fire path ancient desolate beasts that grow large and can self-detonate. Fang Yuan places Canary Pavilion and Chicken Dog Coop as both focused on enslavement path and both rank seven, with Canary Pavilion raising canaries.",
      "chapters": [
        1708
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "emperor-city-fielding",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_emperor_city",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "house_chicken_dog_coop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ye Fan later again names Heavenly Lotus Sect’s Canary Pavilion among Immortal Gu Houses floating over Emperor City.",
      "chapters": [
        1931
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ye-fan-listing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ye_fan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In that later stretch Canary Pavilion again opens bird cages into an overwhelming flock, and Chicken Dog Coop must cooperate with Red River Wheel to resist it.",
      "chapters": [
        1932
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "cage-assault",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_red_river_wheel"
      ]
    }
  ],
